1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,380
Exam tip.

2
00:00:01,380 --> 00:00:07,981
Cardiac output is stroke volume times heart rate, measured in litres per minute, not in beats.

3
00:00:07,981 --> 00:00:13,984
An athlete has a slow pulse but a normal cardiac output, because each beat pumps more.

4
00:00:13,984 --> 00:00:17,330
And normal blood pressure is one twenty over eighty.

